        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Penlee Point, Rame; Plymouth Sound; Cornwall; Doom Bar; River Camel; Celtic Sea\n- Topics: Coastal geography; maritime grounding\n\nFacts:\n- Cornwall is a ceremonial county in the United Kingdom.\n- Penlee Point, Rame is a coastal headland southeast of the village of Rame in southeast Cornwall, UK.\n- Penlee Point, Rame lies at the entrance to Plymouth Sound.\n- Doom Bar, previously called Dunbar sands and similar names, is a sandbar at the mouth of the River Camel estuary where it meets the Celtic Sea on the north coast of Cornwall, England.\n- HMS Whiting grounded on Doom Bar.",
